      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "First, let's find the total distance Ryosuke drove to and from work with his friend. \nThe odometer is 74,568 when Ryosuke picks his friend up and 74,592 when he drops them off, \nso the distance is 74,592 - 74,568 = 24 miles. \nSince Ryosuke drives both ways, the total distance is 24 miles x 2 = 48 miles. \nSince Ryosuke's car gets 28 miles per gallon, he used 48 miles / 28 miles per gallon = 1.714 liters of gas. \nSince the price of one gallon of gas is $4.05, the cost of the gas is 1.714 liters x $4.05 = $6.96. \nHence, the cost of gas that was used for Ryosuke to drive his friend back home from work is \\boxed{\\$6.96}.",
